-- title:
--   Node case: uv=q and generators of mathfrak m_R
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ and let $O^{nr}$ be a characteristic-zero discrete valuation domain which is a $\mathbb Z_q$-algebra, complete for the ideal generated by the image of $q$, that ideal being maximal, and with algebraically closed residue field $k = \mathrm{ResidueField}\,O^{nr}$. Let $\iota : W(\mathbb F_{q^2}) \to O^{nr}$ be a ring homomorphism, written $\mathrm{Zp2}\,q$ for the Witt vectors of the field with $q^2$ elements, and let $X_0$ be a formal $O_D$-module over $k$ (a two-dimensional commutative formal group law with a $W(\mathbb F_{q^2})$-action and a law endomorphism $\varpi$ satisfying $\varpi\circ\varpi = [q]$ and $\varpi\circ a = \sigma(a)\circ\varpi$) which is special for $j = \mathrm{residue}\circ\iota$, i.e. its Lie algebra is the direct sum of the invertible submodules $\mathrm{lieZero}$ and $\mathrm{lieOne}$ on which $a$ acts by $j(a)$ respectively $j(\sigma a)$, and which has height $4$. Let $R$ be a noetherian local $O^{nr}$-algebra, complete for its maximal ideal, let $\mathrm{res}_R : R \to k$ satisfy $\mathrm{res}_R\circ(\text{structure map}) = \mathrm{residue}$, and let $X_u$ be a formal $O_D$-module over $R$ together with an isomorphism $w_u$ from $X_u \otimes_{\mathrm{res}_R} k$ to $X_0$. Assume the pro-representability hypothesis: for every artinian local $O^{nr}$-algebra $A$ with surjective $\mathrm{res}_A : A \to k$ compatible with $\mathrm{residue}$, every formal $O_D$-module $X$ over $A$ that is special for $(\text{structure map})\circ\iota$ and of height $4$, and every isomorphism $w : X\otimes_{\mathrm{res}_A} k \to X_0$, there is a unique $O^{nr}$-algebra map $\chi : R \to A$ with $\mathrm{res}_A\circ\chi = \mathrm{res}_R$ for which some isomorphism $v : X_u\otimes_\chi A \to X$ satisfies $w\circ(v\otimes k) = w_u$ on power series. Assume finally the node condition: the matrix of degree-one coefficients of $\varpi$ on $X_0$ annihilates both $\mathrm{lieZero}$ and $\mathrm{lieOne}$. Then there exist $u, v$ in the maximal ideal of $R$ with $uv$ equal to the image of $q$ in $R$ and $\mathfrak m_R = \mathfrak m_{O^{nr}}R + (u,v) + \mathfrak m_R^2$.
--
--   This is the node (double point) case of Drinfeld's computation of the deformation ring of a special formal $O_D$-module of height $4$: when the linear part of $\varpi$ vanishes on both eigenlines of the Lie algebra, the deformation ring carries two elements with product $q$ whose classes, together with $\mathfrak m_{O^{nr}}$, generate the cotangent space. It feeds the dichotomy statement [`CerednikDrinfeld.SpecialFormalODModule.isRegularLocalRing_and_nonempty_algEquiv_powerSeries_or_uvCrossingModel_of_isProrepresentedBy_deformations`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.SpecialFormalODModule.isRegularLocalRing_and_nonempty_algEquiv_powerSeries_or_uvCrossingModel_of_isProrepresentedBy_deformations), which identifies $R$ either with a formal power series ring or with the crossing model $O^{nr}[[u,v]]/(uv-q)$.
